2,"partTitle":"Appendices and reference","role":"reference"}],"glossary":[{"id":"B06-G1","chapter":27,"term":"Arithmetic intensity","definition":"— The amount of computation performed relative to data movement."},{"id":"B06-G2","chapter":27,"term":"Backpressure","definition":"— A bounded mechanism by which a downstream stage limits upstream production."},{"id":"B06-G3","chapter":27,"term":"Coalescing","definition":"— Combining memory activity from nearby GPU threads into efficient memory transactions when access patterns permit it."},{"id":"B06-G4","chapter":27,"term":"CPU reference implementation","definition":"— A deliberately inspectable implementation used to define expected semantics independently of an optimized GPU path."},{"id":"B06-G5","chapter":27,"term":"Deadline","definition":"— The time by which a unit of work must complete according to a stated requirement."},{"id":"B06-G6","chapter":27,"term":"Device","definition":"— In CUDA terminology, a GPU or other CUDA-capable execution target controlled by host code."},{"id":"B06-G7","chapter":27,"term":"Divergence","definition":"— A condition in which threads executing together follow different control-flow paths, potentially reducing execution efficiency."},{"id":"B06-G8","chapter":27,"term":"End-to-end latency","definition":"— Elapsed time across the complete boundary relevant to the user or system contract, rather than one internal stage."},{"id":"B06-G9","chapter":27,"term":"Heterogeneous computing","definition":"— Computing that deliberately divides work among processors with different architectures or execution characteristics."},{"id":"B06-G10","chapter":27,"term":"Occupancy","definition":"— A CUDA resource and scheduling metric describing active warps relative to architectural limits; it is not a direct measure of useful throughput."},{"id":"B06-G11","chapter":27,"term":"Pinned memory","definition":"— Host memory arranged to support direct asynchronous transfer behavior required by particular CUDA workflows."},{"id":"B06-G12","chapter":27,"term":"Real-time system","definition":"— A system whose correctness includes timing requirements in addition to logical results."},{"id":"B06-G13","chapter":27,"term":"SIMT","definition":"— Single instruction, multiple threads; CUDA's execution model in which threads are grouped for hardware execution while retaining thread-level semantics."},{"id":"B06-G14","chapter":27,"term":"Stream","definition":"— A CUDA ordering domain for asynchronous operations."},{"id":"B06-G15","chapter":27,"term":"Throughput","definition":"— Completed work per unit time under a stated workload."},{"id":"B06-G16","chapter":27,"term":"Warp","definition":"— The hardware execution grouping used by NVIDIA GPUs for CUDA threads."}],"teaching":{},"readingOrder":["B06.C00.T0001","B06.C00.T0002","B06.C00.T0003","B06.C00.T0004","B06.C01.T0005","B06.C01.T0006","B06.C01.T0007","B06.C01.T0008","B06.C01.T0009","B06.C01.T0010","B06.C01.T0011","B06.C01.T0012","B06.C01.T0013","B06.C01.T0014","B06.C01.T0015","B06.C01.T0016","B06.C01.T0017","B06.C01.T0018","B06.C01.T0019","B06.C01.T0020","B06.C01.T0021","B06.C01.T0022","B06.C02.T0023","B06.C02.T0024","B06.C02.T0025","B06.C02.T0026","B06.C02.T0027","B06.C02.T0028","B06.C02.T0029","B06.C02.T0030","B06.C02.T0031","B06.C02.T0032","B06.C02.T0033","B06.C02.T0034","B06.C02.T0035","B06.C02.T0036","B06.C02.T0037","B06.C02.T0038","B06.C02.T0039","B06.C02.T0040","B06.C03.T0041","B06.C03.T0042","B06.C03.T0043","B06.C03.T0044","B06.C03.T0045","B06.C03.T0046","B06.C03.T0047","B06.C03.T0048","B06.C03.T0049","B06.C03.T0050","B06.C03.T0051","B06.C03.T0052","B06.C03.T0053","B06.C03.T0054","B06.C03.T0055","B06.C03.T0056","B06.C03.T0057","B06.C03.T0058","B06.C04.T0059","B06.C04.T0060","B06.C04.T0061","B06.C04.T0062","B06.C04.T0063","B06.C04.T0064","B06.C04.T0065","B06.C04.T0066","B06.C04.T0067","B06.C04.T0068","B06.C04.T0069","B06.C04.T0070","B06.C04.T0071","B06.C04.T0072","B06.C04.T0073","B06.C04.T0074","B06.C04.T0075","B06.C04.T0076","B0